y isn't  always accurate on the PMP and it's  important to keep in mind where we're  getting that information from that  information is reported directly from  dispensers right those are the those are  the pharmacies that are filling and  providing the prescriptions not always  to the hand of the patient in many cases  these patients are in pain and they  don't present at the pharmacy so the  ability to check that check an ID for  legal format a name doesn't go real far  at the pharmacy many times that  information is coming directly from the  prescribers office where that  prescription has been written and this  might be the only place where there's a  veil ability an opportunity to interface  with patient and check ID for the legal  format of the name remember when writing  a prescription that information is going  to be handed off to the pharmacy and  that's the information that it's going  to be reported the PMP it is imperative  that it be accurate that it be the legal  format of the name a good and valid  address when you receive information  back from the PMP that is incorrect or  incomplete we do have a process of  reporting that back to the PMP where we  can followup with the pharmacies to  ensure that the information is corrected  on the PMP you can find a path to that  process on our web page do hy govt slash  PMP thank you I would like to once again  thank Jared Garrity for his presentation  I would also like to thank lab roots for  making today's educational webcast  possible before we go I want to let  everyone know that today's webcast will  be available for on-demand viewing  through February 15 2019 you'll receive  an email from lab roots letting you know  when this webcast will be available for  replay  please share that announcement with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  event that is all for now thank you for  joining us we hope to see you again soon  bye
 

